From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Lay VC-1 pictures out at a 32-byte pitch

VC-1 motion compensation fetches its references at a 32-byte pitch, as
H.264's and HEVC's do. A picture 16 but not 32 aligned in width decoded
its luma exact and its chroma wrong in every inter picture, wrong
differently from run to run where the fetch reached the line padding:
SMPTE's SA00040 (176x144) and SA10091 (720x480).

Lay VC-1 pictures out at a 32-byte pitch too.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
@@ -225,13 +225,14 @@
 	return ALIGN(bytesperline * height * 3 / 2, 256);
 }
 
-/* H.264 and HEVC motion compensation fetches references at a 32-byte pitch. */
+/* H.264, HEVC and VC-1 fetch references at a 32-byte pitch. */
 static inline unsigned int cedrus_picture_stride(struct cedrus_context *ctx,
 						 unsigned int width)
 {
 	switch (ctx->v4l2.format_coded.fmt.pix.pixelformat) {
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC_SLICE:
+	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_SLICE:
 		return ALIGN(width, 32);
 	default:
 		return ALIGN(width, 16);
